Z||000000||XDrewX||11-27-2001||08:17 PM||||I know on my 87 there is a VIN # at the windshield, and on every body panel.<BR>Are the 86 cars the same.?<P>I was always told there were to VIN # plates, one by the windshield and one attached to the engine block.<BR>Is this correct ??<P>Dont ask why I need to know. LOL<P><BR>Thanks<BR>Andrew||||reg||1
Z||000001||jelly2m8||11-27-2001||10:44 PM||||There are 2 VIN plates, one in the windshield like you mentioned, the other is under the dash, on the steering column support bar. If you take the drivers side speaker out and look down you will see it.<P> Engine blocks don't have the vin number on them.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
